{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811613-vii-covenant-discipline-shadow-sorcery","id":811613,"title":"[VII Covenant Discipline] Shadow Sorcery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-19T01:51:14-08:00","id":811613,"title":"[VII Covenant Discipline] Shadow Sorcery","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I am currently planning a Los Angeles-based Mortals --&gt; Vampires Chronicle for 2 players with myself being ST. Now, I don't have experience running Vampire but I have been running CtL 1st Ed for 6 months now and have played VtR 2nd Ed a little bit.<br /> <br /> Here's the deal: I am a really big fan of VII and wanted to make it available as a viable covenant for players that isn't all about being mad. So I came up with something (don't wanna spoil it in case some of the players lurk around here).<br /> <br /> And while doing so, I came up with a basic concept for a discipline that functions in rituals. It's focused on hurting and hunting down Kindred and as such can be devastating to them. Please note, however, that nothing in here is playtested and I do realize that the higher levels might be a little too strong.<br /> <br /> Upcoming spoilers for my players!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Shadow Sorcery<br /> <br /> Shadow Sorcery is VII\u2019s very own form of blood sorcery and a very potent one at that. As Strix hunters, they have learned to use their knowledge of the owls to seize control over aspects of other Kindred or Strix from afar, unleashing their beasts or clouding their senses. It is said that even more terrible forms of Shadow Sorcery have been attempted, such as immediately forcing final death on the target. But if anyone ever succeeded on this, no one knows.<br /> <br /> Shadow Sorcery requires the ritualist to present a tribute, usually one related to the target in question.<br /> <br /> Shadow Sorcery effectively functions as a discipline and as such needs to be purchased in order. Also, ghouls cannot learn Shadow Sorcery as the Vitae used to invoke the rite is spilled onto the magical circle by slitting one\u2019s wrists and violently forces blood out of one\u2019s own body.<br /> The ritualist draws up a magical circle (different for each of the rites) and light seven candles on its edge, placing the tribute in the middle of the circle. Afterwards, he infuses the rite with his Vitae while focusing her mind on the target. If the magical circle was drawn up correctly and the necessary tribute is presented, the rite works as long as the target number of successes is reached on an extended action. The tribute is always consumed in the process, whether or not the rite works out or not.<br /> Purchasing Shadow Sorcery costs 5 Experience points instead of the usual 4 required for other disciplines and requires a mentor or book to learn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Sorcery *: Rite of the shadows gaze:</b><br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Required Successes: 6<br /> 1min/roll<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve + Blood Potency<br /> Tribute: An item or bodypart related to the target (such as a hair of the vampire or her sire, a drop of blood, her touchstone)<br /> <br /> Upon infusing the rite with her own vitae, the user of this ritual marks his targets existence. Once marked, the ritualist can sense the presence of her target within her blood potency in kilometers. This does not give her an exact location but rather a feeling of where she needs to go.<br /> The mark lasts for a number of weeks equal to the ritualists\u2019 blood potency. She may, however, lengthen the duration by infusing the rite with additional vitae. Each additional point of vitae spent gives an additional week. If this is not done upon first casting the rite, another tribute needs to be presented and the full ritual needs to be repeated.<br /> When the ritualist has sight on a marked target, she can make a reflexive Blood Potency + Composure roll to see the targets aura.<br /> Finally, one ritualist may only mark one person at a time. Marking another person will destroy the first mark. Because the mark was infused with Vitae, the ritualist also takes her blood potency in dice as lethal damage while feeling a sharp pain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Sorcery **: Rite of the Clouded Blood:</b><br /> Cost: 2 Vitae<br /> Required Successes: 6<br /> 5min/roll<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve + Blood Potency<br /> Tribute: A human heart not older than 24 hours and a piece of cloth soaked with targets or one of its touchstones\u2019 blood.<br /> <br /> When the ritualist invokes this rite with her own vitae, she clouds the targets senses, making it impossible for the target to see in the dark or to hear a mortal\u2019s heartbeat. The target also cannot sense any Kindred or Strix around it.<br /> This condition lasts for 24 hours once applied and can only affect the target as long as it is within at least one-hundred miles of the ritualist. Otherwise, the rite fails violently, causing the user to take her blood potency in lethal damage.<br /> This rite requires that the target is marked by Rite of the Shadows Gaze.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Sorcery ***: Rite of the Wicked Beast:</b><br /> Cost: 3 Vitae + 1 Willpower<br /> Required Successes: 8<br /> 5min/roll<br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Blood Potency<br /> Tribute: An image of the target\u2019s greatest fear, love, lust or a similarly strong emotion.<br /> <br /> This rite requires the target to be marked by Rite of the Shadows Gaze. Once used, it forces the target into frenzy violently. During this frenzy, the target feels extremely endangered by anyone who surrounds her, causing violent outbursts. This frenzy only ends once the target kills someone or at least one minute passes. After one minute, the target may make a Resolve + Composure (Power + Resistance for Strix) roll to resist the frenzy and return into a controlled state.<br /> <br /> If this rite fails, the ritualist has to succeed on a frenzy check with a -3 modifier or enter frenzy herself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Sorcery ****: Rite of the Bleak River:</b><br /> Cost: 4 Vitae + 1 Willpower<br /> Required Successes: 8<br /> 10min/roll<br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Blood Potency<br /> Tribute: Blood from someone the target fed from in the last week and a bodypart (hair, nail, skin, etc.) of the target or one of his touchstones.<br /> <br /> Once invoked, this rite causes the targeted vampire or Strix to suffer from sudden loss of vitae. Within a moment, the target loses vitae equal to the ritualists\u2019 blood potency (doubled on an exceptional success). If this drains the target of vitae completely, she also immediately loses a point of willpower.<br /> This is one of the most dreaded powers VII uses and one of their primary ways of weakening their victims, as even the strongest elders become much less of a threat when they run out of their precious vitae.<br /> As with all higher level Shadow Sorceries, this requires the target to be marked by Rite of the Shadows Gaze.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Sorcery *****: Work in Progress</b><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","user":"Dragotarify","date":". 01-19-2016, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T02:50:31-08:00","id":811631,"title":"","content":"If anything, this feels too weak.<br /> <br /> The limit of Blood potency is artificial and unneeded in my opinion. The rituals don't do anything fancy to warrant it, and because a lot of the dice pools have Blood Potency in them - elders will be better at it, and neonates will just take longer to cast/will have higher chance of failure. That's enough of a cost imo, without forcing to buy up BP.<br /> <br /> You mentioned Strix, yet there is nothing about it in the game. How about fifth dot, instead of torpor (which is super boring, since if you're the target.. you just get torpored and you have nothing to do), would call a Strix upon the target? With intentions to making things very bad for him. That way, the target has some counter play, the Shadow Sorcery has actual ties with the Strix. <br /> <br /> So someone low in the sorcery can find the victim, later on weaken them. Excellent skills for hunters to have, without instant I win powers like torpor <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:19:04-08:00","id":811664,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well, I wasn't sure about the Blood Potency limitation. I guess you are right that having it affect dice pools should be enough.<br /> <br /> As for the Strix, the point is - Spoiler alert again, dear players - that VII are Strix hunters, meaning they hunt the Strix to lessen their influence on the world and also to learn about them and their relation to the Kindred. So calling them upon a target would actually make very little sense in the context of the background that I worked out for the covenant. The idea of the discipline is to allow the ritualists to hunt down those Kindred who are possessed by the Strix or work for them/worship them. Maybe refocusing the 5th power on actually hurting the Strix themselves would be a good idea, such as ripping them from their possessed body and dealing damage to them in the proccess.<br /> <br /> In addition, one could focus the first power to actually target a strix, not a vampire. This way, one could track down the Strix regardless of which body it is using at the moment. The original idea was to hunt down a vampire affected by the strix but I am starting to think that this would make escaping from the disciplines influence rather easy for the Strix.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I'll take away the BP limitation to start. I'll have to think about changing the powers to be more Strix-related without feeling like they are actually powers of the Strix rather than against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:25:55-08:00","id":811667,"title":"","content":"Oh, sorry, my bad about the strix relation. However, I do think that a devotion or alternative ritual should exist, which would pose serious questions to the practitioners of the power. <br /> <br /> Also, I actually think that the discipline should not differentiate between Strix and Vampires, to muddy the waters just a bit further... &quot;the power designed to fight Strix, actually proves their connection to the vampires&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:33:09-08:00","id":811674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/811613-vii-covenant-discipline-shadow-sorcery?p=811667#post811667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, sorry, my bad about the strix relation. However, I do think that a devotion or alternative ritual should exist, which would pose serious questions to the practitioners of the power.<br /> <br /> Also, I actually think that the discipline should not differentiate between Strix and Vampires, to muddy the waters just a bit further... &quot;the power designed to fight Strix, actually proves their connection to the vampires&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. You mean a devotion that would call upon the Strix? Interesting idea that would allow for inner conflict within the ranks of VII. And would also give a basis for the rumour that VII are actually in some form allied or controlled by the Strix.<br /> <br /> In terms of differentiation: I am going to clear that up. However I am not sure if Strix actually have something akin to frenzy that could be provoked by the 3-dot ritual. Probably need to differentiate between the two for this one or create a similar effect on Strix, such as simply losing control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8604-dragotarify","name":"Dragotarify","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}